[step] The DATA lettering stands 0.48 mm proud of the flat black face. It fills a 0.72 mm recess, the rear chips' raised two-colour lettering (data-ring/README.md), and prints face up in two 0.24 mm layers above the face.
alternatives: Flush lettering gives up the relief that edges the white on the black.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/data-ring/data-ring.step
click: x=5.437 y=2.160 z=14.827

[sliver] The raised lettering's 0.48 mm sidewalls: two ordinary 0.24 mm layers above the flush face on the face-up print.
alternatives: As for the relief: flush lettering removes the sidewalls with the relief.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/data-ring/data-ring.step
click: x=8.730 y=1.920 z=14.895

[ceiling] The linter is wrong for this part's pose. The plate prints flat-back-down with the lettering up (data-ring/README.md), and this face is the 1.68 mm top edge of the RJ11 opening, vertical in the print. The lint reads ceilings only for a piece bedded on its Z- or Z+ face; its ledge reading takes the plate's +Y-up pose.
alternatives: None in the part. The lint could read ceilings in the declared tilted pose, as it reads ledges.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/data-ring/data-ring.step
